moyu (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: the local web server now validates the Host and Origin of every
    request, so a DNS-rebinding page can no longer reach the local API and
    delete book files. Requests from non-loopback hosts are rejected with 403.
  * Performance: parsed books are now kept in a bounded LRU cache (max 4 books
    / 24M characters) instead of growing without limit, and the TUI caches
    layout per terminal width with a debounced resize handler.
  * Tooling: CI runs `tsc --noEmit` on the web frontend, packaging no longer
    skips the build-dependency check, and release builds verify that the tag
    matches debian/changelog.
  * Packaging: add debian/README.Debian explaining the Node.js 22 requirement,
    make the launcher print actionable install hints, and restrict the npm
    tarball to the shipped files.

 -- moyu-reader contributors <moyu-reader@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:16:00 +0800

moyu (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add local web reader with bookshelf, covers, typography settings,
    paged and scrolling modes, and page-turn animations.
  * Add shelf hide (keep file) and permanent local delete actions.
  * Add Markdown reading and web file import for TXT/EPUB/PDF/Markdown.
  * Add `moyu web` command, desktop launcher, moyu:// URL scheme and PWA
    support.

 -- moyu-reader contributors <moyu-reader@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:18:48 +0800

